<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n93154" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σαλμᾰκίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>,
			ἡ, a district in Halicarnassus, <i><span class="en">
			<u>SIG</u>
			46.24
		</span></i>
		<span class="entity">(v B.C.)</span>; also a fountain there, said to cause sexual
		weakness and associated with Hermaphroditus, <i><span class="en">
			Str.
			14.2.16
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Vitr.
			2.8.11
		</span></i>, Ov.<i><span class="en">
			<u>Met.</u>
			4.286
		</span></i>: hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σαλμᾰκίδες</span></b> ,
			αἱ, a name for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑταῖραι</span> (so <i><span class="en">
			Suid.
		</span></i>) or effeminate men, <i><span class="en">
			<u>AP</u>
			7.222
		</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
			Phld.
		</span></i>).</div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
